## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical testing design for event-driven pipelines, focusing on end-to-end integrity, exactly-once semantics, dead-letter queues, and resilience under burst traffic—common challenges in fintech and ride-hailing domains.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture
- Exactly-once processing and idempotency
- Dead-letter queues and backpressure
- Failure injection and chaos testing
- Data integrity validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test: ensure idempotent consumer
let lastProcessed = new Map();
async function process(event) {
  const key = event.id;
  if (lastProcessed.has(key)) {
    return { status: 'duplicate', result: lastProcessed.get(key) };
  }
  const result = await processEvent(event);
  lastProcessed.set(key, result);
  return { status: 'processed', result };
}
```

